## Vue 3

### Component style

- **`<script setup lang="ts">`** only — no Options API in new code
- Type **`defineProps`** and **`defineEmits`**
- **Destructure props** from `defineProps` — set defaults in the destructuring pattern, not via `withDefaults` / `props.foo`; keep `const props = defineProps(...)` only when the whole object is needed (e.g. `v-bind="$props"`)
- Use **`defineModel`** for `v-model` bindings (parent ↔ child)
- Prefer **`computed`** over `watch` when deriving state
- **`defineExpose`** only when parents need imperative access (e.g. `formRef`, `open()`)
- Avoid name shadowing — do not reuse ref names as destructured params
- Wire props through every layer — undeclared props are not passed to children
- Remove `console.log`, `debugger`, and dead code before finishing

### Template & reactivity

- Keep templates declarative; move non-trivial logic to `computed` or functions
- Use `v-if` / `v-show` consistently with neighbouring components
- Prefer `storeToRefs` when destructuring Pinia state in components
- User-facing strings: `useI18n` / `useAppI18n` / `t('key')` — keys in `src/global/locales/en/` — see **`i18n.mdc`**

```vue
<script setup lang="ts">
import { computed } from 'vue';
import { useI18n } from 'vue-i18n';
import type { MessageSchema } from '@/plugins/i18n';

const { t } = useI18n<{ message: MessageSchema }>({ useScope: 'global' });

const { isCreate = false } = defineProps<{ isCreate?: boolean }>();

const emits = defineEmits<{ save: []; cancel: [] }>();
const isOpen = defineModel<boolean>('isOpen', { default: false });
</script>
```

### Composables (`ui/src/composables/`)

- Extract reusable logic into `useXxx.ts`; export from `ui/src/composables/index.ts`
- Name: `use` + PascalCase domain (`useChangeFormDetection`, `useAppI18n`)
- Composables return refs/computed/functions — avoid hidden side effects unless documented
- **Before** writing manual `addEventListener` / resize / storage logic, check if **VueUse** already provides it

#### Do not extract single-use logic

When **creating** or **refactoring** a Vue component, keep logic in the SFC (`<script setup>`) if it is used **only** by that component.

**Do not** add a file under `ui/src/composables/` when:

- The logic has a single consumer (the component being created or refactored)
- Extraction does not enable reuse across components/views

**Extract** a composable only when:

- Two or more components or views need the same logic
- The behavior is shared domain orchestration (match existing `ui/src/composables/` patterns)

For single-use cases, prefer local `computed`, functions, and VueUse primitives in the component — not a dedicated `useXxx.ts`.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — only used in ComplianceProgress.vue
// ui/src/composables/useComplianceProgress.ts
export function useComplianceProgress() { /* ... */ }

// ✅ GOOD — colocated in ComplianceProgress.vue
const progress = computed(() => /* ... */)
async function onSubmit() { /* ... */ }

// ✅ GOOD — shared by Stage1, Stage2, Stage3
// ui/src/composables/useComplianceValidation.ts
```

