## Vue Router

Use **Vue Router** for all in-app navigation — not `window.location`, `history.pushState`, or ad-hoc URL strings.

Setup: `ui/src/router/index.ts` (registered in `ui/src/main.ts`).

### Navigation in components

- **`useRouter()`** / **`useRoute()`** from `vue-router` — not a custom router wrapper
- Prefer **named routes** via `RouterName` — `router.push({ name: RouterName.ENQUIRY_EDIT, params, query })`
- Paths and base segments: **`RouterPathEnum`**, **`RouterPathBaseEnum`** from `@/enums` — do not hardcode URL strings
- Declarative links: **`RouterLink`** / `<router-link>` when the UI is a plain anchor-style navigation
- Route params / query: read from **`useRoute()`** (`route.params`, `route.query`, `route.name`) — do not parse `window.location` manually
- React to param changes with **`watch(() => route.params.xxx, …)`** or `computed` — do not assume `onMounted` runs again on same component instance
- **`router.replace`** when navigation should not add a history entry (e.g. post-login redirect); **`router.push`** for normal navigation
- Unsaved-changes redirects: reuse **`redirectTo`** from `@/utils/util` or **`SweetAlertHelper.redirectPopUp`** when the surrounding file already uses that pattern

```ts
import { useRouter, useRoute } from 'vue-router';
import { RouterName } from '@/enums';

const router = useRouter();
const route = useRoute();

router.push({ name: RouterName.DIARY, params: { mode: 'edit' } });
```

### Adding or changing routes

| Location                       | Role                                                                |
| ------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `ui/src/router/`               | Route modules (`MainRoutes`, `AuthRoutes`, …) and `index.ts` guards |
| `ui/src/enums/router.enum.ts`  | `RouterName`, `RouterPathEnum`, `RouterPathBaseEnum`                |
| `ui/src/config/configPath.ts`  | Main-layout child routes (menu-driven)                              |
| `ui/src/constants/*-routes.ts` | Context-specific route maps (e.g. action-button, customer-text)     |

**Route `meta`** (permissions, auth): set in `configPath.ts` or route modules — e.g. `roleAttributes`, `options`, `requiresAuth`. Do not duplicate permission checks in components when `beforeEach` already handles them.

**Guards & side effects:** global guards live only in `ui/src/router/index.ts` (`beforeEach`, `afterEach`). Route-change domain sync → **`RouterHelper`** — hook from `afterEach`, not scattered in components.

**Lazy routes:** `component: () => import('@/views/...')` — match neighbouring route definitions in `configPath.ts` / `router/`.

Reference: `SaveBanner.vue`, `WhatsNext.vue`, `WidgetModal.vue`, `configPath.ts`.

