## Vuetify 3

Configured in `ui/src/plugins/vuetify.ts` — default theme `LIGHT_THEME`, icon set **MDI** (`mdi-*`).

### Layout & structure

- Grid: `v-container` → `v-row` → `v-col`
- Cards: prefer existing wrappers (`CardItem`, `CustomModal`) over raw `v-card` when they match the screen
- Modals: use **`CustomModal`** for standard dialogs; it wraps `v-dialog` + project header/footer styles
- Loading: `Spinner` / `loader.store` — match surrounding screens

### Form fields (project norm)

Forms and modals commonly override global defaults. Match neighbouring fields in the same file:

| Prop           | Typical value in forms/modals                                            |
| -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| `variant`      | `underlined`                                                             |
| `color`        | `#48a0cc` (brand accent)                                                 |
| `class`        | `font-size-input input-style` (+ `pa-0` where needed)                    |
| `hide-details` | `true` on dense rows; use `:messages` / `:rules` when showing validation |

Global defaults in `vuetify.ts` use `outlined` + `comfortable` — **do not assume** every field uses them; read the file you are editing.

### Validation

- Wrap inputs in **`v-form`** with `ref="formRef"`
- Validate via **`useCheckValidation(formRef)`** from `@/composables` (or `formRef.validate()` when already used locally)
- Rules: `useRules()` from `vuetify/labs/rules` where the file already uses it; pass `t('errors....')` for messages
- Dictionary-driven selects: `item-value="code"`, `item-title="title"` (or `description` — match the data shape)

```vue
<v-form ref="formRef" v-model="formValidate">
  <v-text-field
    v-model="model.name"
    :label="t('name')"
    color="#48a0cc"
    variant="underlined"
    class="font-size-input input-style pa-0"
    hide-details
    :rules="[rules.required(t('errors.fieldIsRequired', { name: t('name') }))]"
  />
</v-form>
```

### Buttons & actions

Match existing action rows:

- Primary save: `class="font-weight-bold text-uppercase btn-default bg-gradient-primary ..."`
- Cancel/plain: `variant="plain"`, `elevation="0"`
- Icon buttons: `mdi-*` via `icon="mdi-..."` or `<v-icon icon="mdi-..." />`
- Uppercase labels for primary actions (`t('actions.save')`, `t('actions.cancel')`)

### Icons

- Default: **MDI** — `mdi-magnify`, `mdi-close`, `mdi-trash-can`, etc.
- Custom icons registered in `vuetify.ts` under `custom` set — use only when already registered

### Theming

- Prefer theme tokens (`primary`, `error`, …) for new generic UI
- Brand accent `#48a0cc` is widely used on form controls — keep consistency in forms
- SCSS overrides live in `ui/src/scss/` — avoid inline styles unless the file already uses them

