## VueUse (`@vueuse/core`)

Dependency is installed; use it for **browser/DOM/reactivity utilities** instead of boilerplate.

### When to use VueUse

| Need                    | Prefer VueUse                          |
| ----------------------- | -------------------------------------- |
| Window/document events  | `useEventListener`                     |
| Viewport / element size | `useWindowSize`, `useElementSize`      |
| Debounce / throttle     | `useDebounceFn`, `useThrottleFn`       |
| Local/session storage   | `useLocalStorage`, `useSessionStorage` |
| Click outside, focus    | `onClickOutside`, `useFocus`           |
| Toggle, async state     | `useToggle`, `useAsyncState`           |

### Project conventions

- Import from **`@vueuse/core`** (e.g. `import { useEventListener } from '@vueuse/core'`)
- Do **not** add manual `window.addEventListener` / `removeEventListener` in new code when VueUse covers the case — see `AddEditEnquiry.vue` (`useEventListener`)
- Domain-specific orchestration stays in `ui/src/composables/`; VueUse primitives can be composed inside those composables
- Do **not** replace existing composables (e.g. `useIsMobile`) with VueUse unless refactoring that area is in scope

```ts
import { useEventListener } from '@vueuse/core';

useEventListener(window, 'keydown', (event) => {
  if (event.key === 'Escape') onClose();
});
```

